	<p class="title">
		Jutta Kleinschmidt
	</p>
	<h2>
		(Germany - 29 August 1962)
	</h2>
	<p>
		From 1987, when she took part in the Pharaohs Rally for the first time, until 1992
		she competed in the motorcycle class in many cross-country rallies and achieved
		a great deal of success. She first competed on four wheels in 1993 as co-driver
		to Jean-Louis Schlesser in the UAE Desert Challenge. The 1994 season saw her debut
		in the Tunisia Rally. From then until 1996 she entered a number of competitions on
		motorcycles and off-road vehicles and achieved many good results. The following year
		she started exclusively in four-wheel-drive cars. She began the Dakar-Agades-Dakar
		Rally with fifth place overall and showed the world what potential she had. In 2001
		the time had come. She achieved her greatest victory: first place at the Dakar.
	</p>
